✂️ vidcuts — Cut Film, Jump-Cuts, Beat Cuts & Silence Remover 🎞️

Usage:
  vidcuts [options] <video...>

Description:
  Erases a chosen percentage of random frames, rhythmic BPM beats, or silent pauses!
  Supports shorter jump-cut timelines, constant-duration freeze-cuts (--mode freeze),
  BPM-synced music cuts (--mode beat), and automatic vlog silence stripping (--mode silence).

Options:
  -p, --percent <N>    Percentage of frames to cut out (1-90, default: 20) 🎯
  -m, --mode <mode>    Cut style (default: frames) 🎬
                       • frames:  Erase random single frames (missing celluloid)
                       • jumps:   Excise micro-chunks (~0.2s jump cuts)
                       • stutter: Rapid 2-frame skips (projector chatter)
                       • freeze:  Drop frames & freeze-hold survivors (keeps original duration & audio!)
                       • beat:    Cut rhythmically in sync with BPM (--bpm or aubio auto-detect)
                       • silence: Auto-strip silent pauses (vlogger / podcast jump-cut editor)
  -i, --interactive    Interactive wizard (prompts for settings & files) 🧙
  --bpm <N>            Target BPM for '--mode beat' 🥁
  --threshold <dB>     Silence threshold in dB for '--mode silence' (default: -38) 🎙️
  --keep-audio         Keep continuous original audio without cutting it 🎵
  --seed <int>         Seed for random cut pattern (reproducible cuts) 🎲
  --jitter             Add mechanical film projector gate weave/jitter 📽️
  --grain              Add analog 16mm/35mm film grain 🎞️
  --flash              Add occasional white splice tape flashes ⚡
  --film-burn          Add warm orange/amber celluloid light-leak burn flashes 🔥
  --scratches          Add vertical 16mm film scratches 🎞️
  --super8             Add dark Super-8 film gate border & optical vignette 🎥
  --mute               Discard audio track from output 🔇
  --from / --to <time> Start/end timestamps ✂️
  -o, --output-dir <d> Write output files to directory 📂
  -f, --force          Overwrite existing output ⚡
  -n, --dry-run        Preview output without running FFmpeg 📝

Short Code Sheet:
  vidcuts -i                                                # interactive guided wizard
  vidcuts --mode silence interview.mp4                      # auto-remove dead air from talking head video
  vidcuts -p 40 --mode freeze --film-burn musicvideo.mp4    # freeze-cuts keeping original song intact
  vidcuts --mode beat --bpm 128 --flash dance.mp4           # rhythmic cuts synced to 128 BPM
  vidcuts -p 20 --jitter --grain --scratches --super8 v.mp4 # full 16mm/Super-8 damaged film look
EOF
